userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add a shared project membership guard on specified slug routes and refuse project VIEWER on KB writes.

**Motivation** — Since #139 created real `ProjectMember` rows, a non-member DEVELOPER can still read and write every ticket in every project.

**Approach** — Partial extension of existing `apps/api` modules. No new package. `ProjectAccessService.findProjectIdBySlug(slug): Promise<string>` throws `NotFoundAppException` for an unknown or soft-deleted project; `ProjectAccessService.assertProjectMembership(projectId, principal): Promise<void>` returns for agents and global ADMIN users and throws `ForbiddenAppException` for a user with no `ProjectMember` row. `ProjectAccessModule` exports `ProjectAccessService`; `@Principal()` reads `request.user`, and the global `CombinedAuthGuard` is registered before route guards run. Add `ProjectAccessService.findMembershipRole(projectId, userId): Promise<string | null>` as a thin wrapper over existing `PrismaProjectRepository.findMembershipRole`; provide/export `ProjectMembershipGuard` in ProjectAccessModule. Applied with `@UseGuards(ProjectMembershipGuard)`: TicketsController (`projects/:slug/tickets`) class; LabelsController routes under `projects/:slug/...` methods; CommentsController `projects/:slug/tickets/:ref/comments` POST/GET methods; RagController (`projects/:slug/kb`) class; ProjectsController GET `:slug` and PATCH `:slug/agents/:agentSlug` methods. Import ProjectAccessModule in CommentsModule, LabelsModule and RagModule; TicketsModule has access through ProjectsModule. Remove inline project lookup/membership calls from TicketsController.assign. RagController writes `POST documents`, `DELETE documents/:sourceId`, `POST import/graphify`, `POST optimize` carry `@ProjectRoles('ADMIN', 'DEVELOPER', 'AGENT')`; KB reads/search permit project VIEWER. Update existing direct-controller specs for the guard/handler boundary.

**Interface** — verbatim design algorithm:
```typescript
// projects/project-roles.decorator.ts
export const PROJECT_ROLES_KEY = 'koda:projectRoles';
export const ProjectRoles = (...roles: string[]) => SetMetadata(PROJECT_ROLES_KEY, roles);

// projects/project-membership.guard.ts
@Injectable()
export class ProjectMembershipGuard implements CanActivate {
  constructor(private readonly access: ProjectAccessService, private readonly reflector: Reflector) {}

  async canActivate(ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<boolean> {
    const req = ctx.switchToHttp().getRequest();
    const slug = req.params?.slug;
    if (!slug) return true; // routes without :slug are gated elsewhere
    const projectId = await this.access.findProjectIdBySlug(slug); // 404
    await this.access.assertProjectMembership(projectId, req.user); // 403
    const roles = this.reflector.getAllAndOverride<string[]>(PROJECT_ROLES_KEY, [ctx.getHandler(), ctx.getClass()]);
    if (roles?.length && isUserPrincipal(req.user) && req.user.role !== 'ADMIN') {
      const role = await this.access.findMembershipRole(projectId, req.user.id);
      if (!role || !roles.includes(role)) throw new ForbiddenAppException({}, 'projects'); // 403
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

**Scope** — In: specified previously ungated slug routes, KB write-role exception and ticket assign inline-check removal. Out: slug-less comment mutations and project list (US-002), RetrievalController migration and duplicate-check removal (US-005), already gated/ADMIN-permission routes. Project-role-based permissions: write permissions stay on the principal's global role and `ProjectMember.role` gates visibility only (Track 3 ruling 2026-09-27), with one exception ruled 2026-09-27: KB write routes refuse a project VIEWER via `@ProjectRoles`. Tickets, comments and labels do not use `@ProjectRoles`.
